From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 21:46:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/21] wayland: let the shell magnify windows without blurring
 them

A shell that zooms its windows past their size shows their buffers
stretched, which blurs text and lines.

A window's magnification property tells the compositor how much larger
than its size it is shown. Wayland clients are asked for that much more
detail through the fractional and integer preferred buffer scales of
the window's surfaces, so a magnified window stays sharp. Popups and
dialogs follow their parent window. Unconstrained windows that lie
beyond every monitor take the primary monitor's scale, since the shell
shows them there.
